            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-42282",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-42282: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2023-42282?s=github&n=ip&t=npm&vr=%3D2.0.0",
              "help": {
                "text": "The `isPublic()` function in the NPM package `ip` doesn't correctly identify certain private IP addresses in uncommon formats such as `0x7F.1` as private. Instead, it reports them as public by returning `true`. This can lead to security issues such as Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) if `isPublic()` is used to protect sensitive code paths when passed user input. Versions 1.1.9 and 2.0.1 fix the issue.\n",
                "markdown": "> The `isPublic()` function in the NPM package `ip` doesn't correctly identify certain private IP addresses in uncommon formats such as `0x7F.1` as private. Instead, it reports them as public by returning `true`. This can lead to security issues such as Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) if `isPublic()` is used to protect sensitive code paths when passed user input. Versions 1.1.9 and 2.0.1 fix the issue.\n\n|                                  |\n|Package         pkg:npm/ip@2.0.0  |\n|Affected range  =2.0.0            |\n|Fixed version   2.0.1             |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "=2.0.0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "fixed_version": "2.0.1",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:npm/ip@2.0.0"
                ],
                "security-severity": "3.1",
                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-5889",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-5889: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2025-5889?s=github&n=brace-expansion&t=npm&vr=%3E%3D2.0.0%2C%3C%3D2.0.1",
              "help": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in juliangruber brace-expansion up to 1.1.11/2.0.1/3.0.0/4.0.0. It has been rated as problematic. Affected by this issue is the function expand of the file index.js. The manipulation leads to inefficient regular expression complexity. The attack may be launched remotely. The complexity of an attack is rather high. The exploitation is known to be difficult. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. Upgrading to version 1.1.12, 2.0.2, 3.0.1 and 4.0.1 is able to address this issue. The name of the patch is `a5b98a4f30d7813266b221435e1eaaf25a1b0ac5`. It is recommended to upgrade the affected component.\n",
                "markdown": "> A vulnerability was found in juliangruber brace-expansion up to 1.1.11/2.0.1/3.0.0/4.0.0. It has been rated as problematic. Affected by this issue is the function expand of the file index.js. The manipulation leads to inefficient regular expression complexity. The attack may be launched remotely. The complexity of an attack is rather high. The exploitation is known to be difficult. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. Upgrading to version 1.1.12, 2.0.2, 3.0.1 and 4.0.1 is able to address this issue. The name of the patch is `a5b98a4f30d7813266b221435e1eaaf25a1b0ac5`. It is recommended to upgrade the affected component.\n\n|                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n|Package                                                                                                                                                                                                          pkg:npm/brace-expansion@2.0.1  |\n|Affected range                                                                                                                                                                                                   >=2.0.0,<=2.0.1                |\n|Fixed version                                                                                                                                                                                                    2.0.2                          |\n|[[CVSS Score 1.3] [CVSS Vector CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X]]                                 |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">=1.0.0,<=1.1.11",
                "cvssV3": 1.3,
                "cvssV3_severity": "LOW",
                "cvssV3_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:P/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X",
                "fixed_version": "1.1.12",
                "purls": [
